      "id": "q08",
      "answer": "Evidenced direct production consumers: OwnerController (constructor injection; prefix search, findById, save), PetController (constructor injection; findById and saveAndFlush), and VisitController (constructor injection; findById and save). Those are concrete dependency edges. Changing the prefix method directly concerns owner search; it does not alone prove behavioral changes in pet or visit flows, which use other repository methods. Interface-wide or persistence changes might affect them depending on the change. Exhaustiveness beyond these inspected production classes is unverified.",
